A||N||2||huggy||Altenator replacement on 84 automatic||||9||
Z||000000||huggy||09-12-2000||12:21 PM||||Ok I have the oil filter removed, the altenator bracket removed car is up on ramps<BR>the altenator is free but I can't find an <BR>opening big enough to get the altenator out<BR>from the bottom. Please help before I go crazy.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-12-2000||12:35 PM||||Take the dogbone off at the motor/alt bracket and the upper alt. mount off it will come right out the top. I have doen this 3 times and it was only hard the first time I got the hang of it now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I never tried it out the bottom before.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-12-2000||12:35 PM||||On my 87 I passed it under the manifold toward the tranny. It's a tight fit. (You can't take the bracket off on 87.)<P>If the dog bone doesn't give you enough room room, undo the rear tranny mount so you can tip the motor forward. (87's have differant mounts and are easier to tip than your 84)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-12-2000).]||||reg||1
